{{!--
AGENTS.hbs — personal global rules template for the Zed agent.

When this file exists and renders successfully, its output replaces the
verbatim `AGENTS.md` injection in the agent's system prompt. On a render
error Zed falls back to `AGENTS.md` and shows a warning. Delete this file
to return to plain `AGENTS.md` behavior entirely.

Text is emitted verbatim — anything that isn't a `{{...}}` mustache lands in
the prompt unchanged. Comments like this one are stripped at render time and
never reach the model.

Context variables:
  available_tools   names of the tools enabled for this session
  model_name        active model name, if any
  date              today's date, YYYY-MM-DD
  is_windows        host platform gates
  is_linux
  is_macos
  sandboxing        whether terminal commands run in the OS-level sandbox

Helpers: `contains`, plus the built-in boolean helpers `and`, `or`,
`not`, `eq`, `ne`, `gt`, `lt`, `len`, nestable as subexpressions:

  {{#if (contains available_tools 'grep')}}
  Prefer the `grep` tool for content search.
  {{/if}}
  {{#if (and (contains available_tools 'grep') (contains available_tools 'terminal'))}}
  Never run grep through the `terminal` tool.
  {{/if}}

Blocks also work inline — `a {{#if is_windows}}x{{/if}} b` splices `x`
mid-line. There is no ternary form: `{{if cond "yes" "no"}}` parses but
renders nothing — always use the block.

Partials (imports): every `*.hbs` file under this directory (recursively) is
importable by its relative path without the extension, `/`-separated on
every platform — `partials/style.hbs` → `{{> partials/style}}`. Use `/` even
on Windows: `\` is the template escape character and cannot appear in a
partial name. This file is self-contained and no longer splices `AGENTS.md`.
